WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.810
- [Narrator] Take a look at
this satellite image from China.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.700
At first glance, it shows nothing

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.420
but an empty, arid, desert landscape,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.750
but right in the middle
there's something unusual,

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.433
some kind of structure.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.090
As we zoom in, we can see

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.520
it looks just like an aircraft carrier,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.830
the kind used by
militaries around the world

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.360
as floating air bases

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.440
complete with runways,
fighter jets and weapons.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.570
But this one isn't in the ocean,

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.673
but in the middle of the desert.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.813
Let's zoom out for some context.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.700
The satellite image was taken
over to Taklamakan Desert

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.203
in Northwestern China.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.410
Normally, aircraft carriers operate

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.963
in the harsh conditions of the open sea,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.353
but this region, while far
more dry, is no less extreme.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.410
From a global perspective,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.130
the Taklamakan Desert
is a fascinating place.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.400
Unlike the surrounding
deserts made of rock,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.770
this one is made of sand.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:12.540
In fact, it is the second
largest sand desert in the world.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:16.410
Vast, uninhabited and
seemingly untouched by humans,

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.550
it stretches out like a
giant eye made of sand,

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.260
a landscape so alien,

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.173
it almost looks like it
belongs to another planet.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.620
So why, of all places,

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.653
would the Chinese military
built these structures here?

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.990
In recent years, China has
made increasing headlines

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.930
for its expanding
aircraft carrier project.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.230
- China's first domestically-built
aircraft carrier

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.060
has entered service.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.620
- China has clearly invested

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.990
in this defense industrial infrastructure

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.760
to produce these ships.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.170
- [Narrator] Just 15 years ago,

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.320
China didn't have a
single aircraft carrier.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.480
Today it has three.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.790
But if we take a closer look at the shape

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:03.033
in the satellite image,
something doesn't add up.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:07.650
The design doesn't match
that of China's own carriers.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.530
Instead, the structure
strongly resembles the design

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.570
of the American ones.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.540
For comparison, here is
the distinctive shape

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.970
of the Gerald R. Ford-class carrier,

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.583
the latest in the US Navy's fleet.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.120
Moving slightly away from this location,

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.840
we can see a path cutting
through the desert.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.330
This appears to be train tracks

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.310
and on the other side of the tracks,

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.833
yet another structure comes into view.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.240
This one doesn't look
like an aircraft carrier,

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.130
but it has a striking resemblance

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.530
to an Arleigh Burke-class destroyer,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.893
one of the most widely used
warships in the US Navy.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.490
The similarity is unmistakable,

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.620
not just because of its general shape,

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.800
but because of the precise
outlines of key features,

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.380
like the ship's bridge, its funnels,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.690
and even the vertical launch system

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.060
used for firing missiles.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.660
But it also doesn't look
quite like the real ship.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.270
It looks more like a flat mock-up,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.513
a replica built to mimic the real thing.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.720
Examining historical satellite images

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.910
confirms this suspicion.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:24.180
We can see that in 2020,
the site first appeared

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.840
as a grid of cubes with
several tall structures,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.240
possibly masts or antennas

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.810
arranged in the shape
of the American warship.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.450
Only later, the full outline of the ship

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.133
was marked more clearly.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.720
The aircraft carrier shape

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.660
also appears to be just a mock-up.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.050
Here, older satellite images
show that this spot originally

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.820
had a different layout,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:53.100
featuring three distinct shapes,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:57.480
a small and a medium sized
outline of an aircraft carrier

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.473
and the largest version drawn
with those tall metal poles.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.920
And when we look again at the train tracks

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.180
running through the middle,

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.390
we can see just how strange they are.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:13.320
Instead of running straight,
the track curves and twists

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.723
before making a sharp right turn.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.960
This is odd because the surrounding desert

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.880
is completely flat land,

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.610
so there are absolutely
no natural obstacles

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.580
that would require these turns.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.880
Why wasn't the track
built in a straight line?

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.260
And it gets even stranger

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.900
when we follow where these tracks lead.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.230
Heading north, they come to
a stop at a base facility

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.690
with a large hangar,

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:43.323
a few supporting buildings
and a lot of trucks nearby.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:50.370
And when following the tracks
the other way heading south,

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:55.370
they simply vanish into the
desert as the tracks just end,

00:04:55.950 --> 00:05:00.543
with no sign of ongoing
construction and no clear purpose.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.940
To get close to understanding why China

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.530
is doing all of this,

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.860
it's helpful to take a look
at where the real counterparts

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.860
of these mock-up ships are located

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:16.770
because it turns out US aircraft carriers

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.560
often aren't as far away from this desert

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.510
as one might think.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:22.343
- [Reporter 1] The United States

00:05:22.343 --> 00:05:25.080
has deployed an aircraft
carrier to the South China Sea.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.430
- [Reporter 2] A Chinese warship

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.750
almost running into an
American destroyer on Saturday.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.670
- [Narrator] Tensions in
the waters around China

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.470
have been escalating for years,

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:38.580
leading to frequent confrontation
between the US and China.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:41.970
At the center of these disputes
are two major conflicts,

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.853
the South China Sea and Taiwan.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.750
In the South China Sea,
multiple nations lay claim

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.240
to various overlapping territories

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:55.110
and China asserts its claim
over almost the entire sea,

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:58.440
treating the ocean as its
own national territory

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.633
rather than international waters.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.180
To reinforce this claim,

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.660
China has artificially
expanded low-lying islands

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.990
and underwater reefs,
covering them with sand

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:13.770
and transforming them
into military outposts.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.240
The US in response

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.850
regularly sends warships
through these waters

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:21.060
and conducts military exercises.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.170
The purpose of these

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:24.600
so-called freedom of navigation operations

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.903
is to challenge China's
territorial claims on the sea.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.180
But this is just one
reason why US carriers

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.400
are present near China.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.870
The second major conflict

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.730
is the increasingly tense situation

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.890
between China and Taiwan.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.350
- [Reporter 3] Tensions
over Taiwan look no closer

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.000
to a peaceful resolution.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.440
- [Reporter 4] Beijing claims Taiwan

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.330
as part of its territory.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.520
- [Narrator] While Taiwan defacto operates

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.880
as a fully independent nation
with its own government,

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.450
mainland China views it
as a renegade province,

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.190
one that if necessary,

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.623
could be brought under control by force.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:08.670
The threat of a Chinese
invasion of Taiwan is very real

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.430
and it is something the US opposes,

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.760
which is why the US Navy
maintains a strong presence

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.980
in the Taiwan Strait,

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.800
two serious conflicts
that have the potential

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.720
to become much worse

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.690
and China is preparing for
them by using their desert

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:28.770
as a practice ground for
a potential future war.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.170
The structures are practice targets

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.420
built to test whether Chinese missiles

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.513
can accurately strike US warships.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:38.820
Some experts believe

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:42.480
that the many vertical
metal poles could be sensors

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.360
used to study the impact
of missile strikes

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.160
on these targets.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.490
Another theory is that
they are radar reflectors

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.790
placed to better simulate
the complex metal structure

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.200
of an actual vessel

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.083
so that radar guided
attacks can be tested.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:03.300
And satellite images from a
different test site confirms

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.613
China is hitting their targets.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.360
But striking a stationary
target is one thing.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:16.560
A real warship, of course,
wouldn't just sit still,

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.563
and that is where the train
tracks come into play.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.010
When following the exact
path of the tracks,

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:26.370
we find yet another
aircraft carrier mock-up,

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:29.610
this one perhaps the most
elaborate of them all,

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.920
a three dimensional model complete

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.623
with numerous poles sticking
up from its structure.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.450
A photograph taken at a
Chinese arms convention appears

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.540
to show a scale model of this very system.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.890
And according to these photos,

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.420
the mock-up was developed

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.063
by the Chinese arms manufacturer, CASIC.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.170
Experts believe that the curves
in the track are designed

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.650
so China can simulate
a United States carrier

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:59.103
taking evasive maneuvers
to avoid being hit.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.690
They can simulate a carrier
taking two sharp turns

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.150
to avoid being tracked by a missile

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:10.383
or speeding off to get out
of the possible impact zone.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.340
And once again, satellite imagery suggests

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.683
that these tests have been successful.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.410
Now, China isn't the only
country building mock-ups

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.480
of American warships.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.900
In 2014, Iran constructed a replica

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:32.900
of a US aircraft carrier,
this one even seaworthy.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.980
They used it for missile tests

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:38.130
and then repeatedly
bombed it until it sank,

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:41.790
an exercise that gained
international media attention.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.820
Even though propaganda may
have played a larger role

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.700
than actual practice
in this specific case,

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.090
training with mock-up targets
is a common military practice,

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:53.520
and the US is doing this all the time,

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.360
building elaborate fake
towns in their own deserts

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.900
and even training with their own mock-ups.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:05.280
For instance, a replica of
China's Chengdu J-20 fighter jet

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:09.000
was spotted at a US Air
Force base in Georgia,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.490
and it's well documented
that the US military

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:14.480
has operated fully
functional Russians Su-27

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:18.150
and the MiG-29 fighter
jets on American soil

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.980
for training purposes.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:21.390
But what makes these mock-ups

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.490
particularly concerning for the US

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:27.510
is that China isn't
testing ordinary weapons.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:30.870
China is using these tests
to demonstrate a system

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.600
that could fundamentally
change military strategy

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.943
in both conflicts mentioned before.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.480
US intelligence assumes

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:42.060
that China possesses a specialized variant

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.400
of its Dongfeng 21D missile

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.040
that is specifically designed to target

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.486
and destroy moving warships
like aircraft carriers.

00:10:50.486 --> 00:10:53.310
(missile roaring)

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:56.790
This Chinese missile follows
a ballistic trajectory,

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.710
launching high into the atmosphere

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:02.670
before plummeting back
down at extreme speeds.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.650
Then, during the descent phase,

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:08.997
a maneuverable reentry vehicle
separates from the missile.

00:11:08.997 --> 00:11:11.910
And unlike a traditional
ballistic war head,

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:15.120
this one can adjust its course in midair,

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:19.110
allowing it to strike
smaller, more precise targets

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:22.053
and even track and hit moving ships.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.790
To support this system,

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:30.060
China has also expanded
its satellite network,

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:35.010
improving its ability to track
moving targets in real time.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:38.460
Experts believe that defending
against this kind of weapon

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.770
is extremely difficult.

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:43.410
Unlike short range missiles or torpedoes,

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:46.320
which require a submarine
to get dangerously close

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:47.820
to an aircraft carrier,

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:50.970
this system enables
China to attack US ships

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:54.270
from medium range in mainland China.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.810
This means conventional US
surface-to-air defense systems

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.360
may not be able to react quickly enough

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.570
to intercept the missile
during the mid-flight phase.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:04.830
And in the final phase,

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.200
interception becomes even more difficult

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.540
due to the maneuverable reentry vehicle,

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.060
which follows an unpredictable flight path

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:15.453
and could potentially
execute evasive maneuvers.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.590
Conducting these tests in
the middle of the desert

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:21.360
fully visible to satellites

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.090
could be seen as an intentional message,

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.860
as it is to the benefit of China

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.710
if these capabilities are known.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:31.860
That is, because the mere
existence of this technology

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:35.610
is already shifting the balance of power.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.770
If the US cannot bring their carriers

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.230
within striking distance of missile,

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:44.010
they are forced to operate
them farther away from China,

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:46.950
which would put the conflict
zones outside the range

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:49.470
of the aircraft stationed on the carrier,

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:53.190
practically negating the
use of such carriers.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:56.280
And so, without ever
needing to use the weapon,

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:59.670
its presence is
strengthening China's ability

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.973
to project power in these conflict zones.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:08.250
Taiwan is also preparing
for this possibility

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.083
and the country

00:13:09.083 --> 00:13:12.420
has recently announced a
large scale military drill,

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:15.870
simulating a Chinese
invasion of the island,

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.563
with over 22,000 reservists taking part.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.490
So far, this story hasn't been picked up

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.980
by many major US news outlets,

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.680
but it's an important
development to follow.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.890
And to help myself keep
track of stories like this,

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:35.820
I love using this video's
sponsor, Ground News.

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:38.340
The idea behind Ground News is simple,

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.630
but it completely changed

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.303
how I stay on top of global events.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.310
Ground News doesn't
write its own articles.

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:51.030
Instead, it collects coverage
from a wide range of sources

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.820
and organizes them by story.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:55.350
At the top of each story,

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.870
you get a quick summary
of what's going on.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.420
You can instantly see how coverage differs

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.570
between left and right-leaning sources.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.310
In this case, Ground News shows

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:09.180
that the Taiwan story has
been covered by 23 sources,

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:14.180
36% left, 43% center, and 21% right.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.530
Bloomberg, a left-leaning outlet,

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.480
frames the drills as President Lai

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.310
choosing to confront China,

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:23.910
implying Taiwan is provoking tension.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:24.743
On the right,

00:14:24.743 --> 00:14:28.590
